<title>UK: UK October car sales rise lifts year-to-date total.</title>
<headline>UK October car sales rise lifts year-to-date total.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON, DATE</dateline>
<text>
<p>British new car sales</p>
<p> OCTOBER			154,733 vs 136,605   - up 13.27 pct</p>
<p> 1996 Yr to date	  1,811,967 vs 1,730,771 - up  4.69 pct</p>
<p> Total yr to date by marque, mkt share in pct vs year ago</p>
<p> Ford	   360,139 (19.88 pct) vs 369,031 (21.32 pct)</p>
<p> GM  Vauxhall 254,707 (14.06 pct) vs 261,011 (15.08 pct)</p>
<p> Rover Group  190,044 (10.49 pct) vs 199,296 (11.51 pct)</p>
<p> Peugeot	136,855  (7.55 pct) vs 129,986  (7.51 pct)</p>
<p> Renault	121,238  (6.69 pct) vs 111,188  (6.42 pct)</p>
<p> VW	     102,206  (5.64 pct) vs 72,196   (4.17 pct)</p>
<p> Nissan	  84,081  (4.64 pct) vs 81,764   (4.72 pct)</p>
<p> Fiat	    76,064  (4.20 pct) vs 62,888   (3.63 pct)</p>
<p> Citroen	 69,873  (3.86 pct) vs 72,467   (4.19 pct)</p>
<p> Toyota	  55,422  (3.06 pct) vs 49,239   (2.84 pct)</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
